    {"id":"AccountSwitchOffAfterDeletion","text":"Cloud save is off; you can turn it on again in Settings."},
    {"id":"PrivacyParagraphCloud","text":"The game opens an invisible player account for you. It asks for no name, email or password; a random player ID identifies the account. Your progress, your wallet and the list of your purchases are kept in this account on the servers of Unity Gaming Services; Unity provides this service on our behalf. So when you reinstall the game or change phones, you carry on where you left off. Without internet the game plays just the same; your save syncs once you are back online. Your settings, your statistics choice and your attempt records stay on this phone only. You can turn the cloud save off with the Cloud save switch in Settings; the game then connects to no account and syncs nothing."},
    {"id":"PrivacyParagraphPlatform","text":"If Google Play Games (Game Center on iPhone and iPad) is on on your phone, your account is linked to it. For this, Google or Apple confirms your player ID in this game to Unity; your name, email and friends list never reach the game. If you don’t link it, your account knows this phone only."},
    {"id":"PrivacyParagraphVerification","text":"To tell that a purchase is real, the game sends the purchase record the store gave (the product, the order ID and the store’s signed record) to our server code at Unity. The server asks Google Play or Apple about it and keeps the result in your account. Refunded purchases are marked in this list."}
  ]
